{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "t001",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# 06 · RESEARCH ARCHIVE — what we know, how, and how confident",
      "x": -1100,
      "y": -1450,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "#a16207"
    },
    {
      "id": "t002",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## RESEARCH ARCHIVE\nThe R307S is the most investigated object in this project\nand the one we understand least.\n[[06 - Research Archive/Research Archive.md]]",
      "x": -1100,
      "y": -1280,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 170,
      "color": "#a16207"
    },
    {
      "id": "g003",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "R307S IDENTITY + PINOUT  —  FAMILY-LEVEL, NOT THIS BOARD",
      "x": -300,
      "y": -1450,
      "width": 2400,
      "height": 250,
      "color": "#92400e"
    },
    {
      "id": "t004",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**1 VCC**  4.2–6.0 V DC\n(1 listing claims 3.6 V min)",
      "x": -270,
      "y": -1370,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "#92400e"
    },
    {
      "id": "t005",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**2 GND**\n",
      "x": 250,
      "y": -1370,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "#92400e"
    },
    {
      "id": "t006",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**3 TXD** out of the module",
      "x": 770,
      "y": -1370,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "#c2410c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t007",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**4 RXD** into the module",
      "x": 1290,
      "y": -1370,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "#c2410c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t008",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**5 TOUCH out** HIGH when a finger is present, only if **6** is powered · **6 touch-sense power** 3.3–5 V, ~5 µA · ~50 mA typ / 80 mA peak · onboard 3.3 V LDO + Synochip AS606 + TTP233D · **no power LED, only blue illumination**",
      "x": -270,
      "y": -1230,
      "width": 2060,
      "height": 90,
      "color": "#a16207"
    },
    {
      "id": "t009",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### The jumper that can silently kill it\n**open** (factory) → pin 1 feeds the LDO, 5 V expected\n**shorted** → LDO bypassed, pin 1 **must** be 3.3 V\n**5 V into a shorted jumper = silent death.**",
      "x": -270,
      "y": -1120,
      "width": 1030,
      "height": 130,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t010",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### USB 2.0 interface\nEnumerates as a PC virtual COM port.\nOn the R307S it is **4 unpopulated solder pads in UNVERIFIED order**.\nThe single highest-value untried test — and it needs equipment.",
      "x": 800,
      "y": -1120,
      "width": 1030,
      "height": 130,
      "color": "#0891b2"
    },
    {
      "id": "g011",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "PROTOCOL  —  UART 8-N-1, default 57600 (=9600×6)",
      "x": -1100,
      "y": -950,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 560,
      "color": "#15803d"
    },
    {
      "id": "t012",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "```\n EF 01 │ 32-bit address │ PID │ len(2) │ content │ checksum(2)\n        default 0xFFFFFFFF\n```\nPID  01 cmd · 02 data · 07 ACK · 08 end\nchecksum = sum(PID+len+content) mod 2¹⁶",
      "x": -1070,
      "y": -870,
      "width": 1030,
      "height": 150,
      "color": "#15803d"
    },
    {
      "id": "t013",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**A mismatched address is ignored in complete silence** — indistinguishable from a dead sensor over the wire.\nDefault password `0x00000000`. Touch circuitry is irrelevant to UART.",
      "x": -1070,
      "y": -690,
      "width": 1030,
      "height": 130,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t014",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Valid baud set is exactly **9600 × N, N = 1…12**. All 12 were tried. **0 bytes at every one.**",
      "x": -1070,
      "y": -530,
      "width": 1030,
      "height": 110,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t015",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Capacity disputed:** 1000 (datasheet) vs 300 (retail listing). Only ReadSysPara settles it — and it never ran.",
      "x": -1070,
      "y": -420,
      "width": 1030,
      "height": 90,
      "color": "#92400e"
    },
    {
      "id": "g016",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "THE EVIDENCE CHAIN  —  full matrix in `docs/r307s-test-matrix.md`",
      "x": 400,
      "y": -950,
      "width": 2000,
      "height": 560,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t017",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**HW-02** — TX 16 B → RX 0 B",
      "x": 430,
      "y": -870,
      "width": 1200,
      "height": 88,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t018",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**HW-03** — 0 bytes at all 12 bauds → baud EXCLUDED",
      "x": 430,
      "y": -770,
      "width": 1200,
      "height": 88,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t019",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**HW-11** — 0 bytes, swapped routing → crossed wires EXCLUDED",
      "x": 430,
      "y": -670,
      "width": 1200,
      "height": 88,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t020",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**HW-13** — RX line **driven high** → not floating",
      "x": 430,
      "y": -570,
      "width": 1200,
      "height": 88,
      "color": "#92400e"
    },
    {
      "id": "t021",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**HW-05/06** — ReadSysPara / TemplateCount NOT EXECUTED",
      "x": 430,
      "y": -470,
      "width": 1200,
      "height": 88,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t022",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**HW-10** — USB pads NOT EXECUTED",
      "x": 430,
      "y": -370,
      "width": 1200,
      "height": 88,
      "color": "#525252"
    },
    {
      "id": "t023",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### What HW-13 means\n\nDriving high under **both** pull-down and pull-up, 200/200 samples, rules out a floating wire.\n\nIt is **not** a calibrated voltage, does not identify the driver, and says **nothing** about the supply rail. A dead UART with a live output stage looks identical.",
      "x": 1700,
      "y": -870,
      "width": 670,
      "height": 260,
      "color": "#92400e"
    },
    {
      "id": "g024",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "STILL OPEN  —  six questions no software can answer",
      "x": -1100,
      "y": -320,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 480,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t025",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "1 · Is the module powered? (meter on pin 1)",
      "x": -1070,
      "y": -240,
      "width": 1030,
      "height": 62,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t026",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "2 · Is the 3.3 V jumper open or shorted?",
      "x": -1070,
      "y": -170,
      "width": 1030,
      "height": 62,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t027",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "3 · Is the TX high level safe for a 3.3 V GPIO?",
      "x": -1070,
      "y": -100,
      "width": 1030,
      "height": 62,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t028",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "4 · Do the harness wires contact the pads believed?",
      "x": -1070,
      "y": -30,
      "width": 1030,
      "height": 62,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t029",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "5 · Is the ESP32-TX → sensor-RX conductor intact? *(never tested independently)*",
      "x": -1070,
      "y": 40,
      "width": 1030,
      "height": 62,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "t030",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "6 · Does the module boot, and with what address/password?",
      "x": -1070,
      "y": 110,
      "width": 1030,
      "height": 62,
      "color": "#b91c1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "g031",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "OTHER RESEARCH THREADS",
      "x": 400,
      "y": -320,
      "width": 2000,
      "height": 480,
      "color": "#a16207"
    },
